{
  "manufacturer": "Invertek Drives",
  "manufacturer_slug": "invertek-drives",
  "model": "Optidrive Coolvert compressor drive (built-in Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "optidrive-coolvert",
  "short_model": "Optidrive Coolvert",
  "aliases": [
    "Optidrive CoolVert",
    "Coolvert"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "Invertek Optidrive Coolvert HVAC compressor drives on the terminal or RJ45 Modbus RTU port, per user guide version 2.01.",
  "summary": "The Optidrive Coolvert is Invertek's variable speed drive for refrigeration and HVAC compressors (BLDC, PM, induction and synchronous reluctance). Modbus RTU is built in on control terminals 1-3 and the RJ45 port. Registers 1-5 take the control word, speed set point in rps and ramp time; registers 7-45 report speed, current, power, trip codes, energy and run time. Every parameter also has its own register (P1-11 = 111).",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 115200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The guide numbers registers from 1 and tells masters that start at register 0 to subtract 1, so control word register 1 is wire address 0. Parameters use their group and number as the register (P6-04 = register 604 = wire address 603)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Optidrive Coolvert User Guide",
    "doc_number": "Version 2.01",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.invertekdrives.com/downloads/Optidrive%20Coolvert%20User%20Guide%20V2.01.pdf",
    "pages": "5.5 Modbus connections and telegram structure pp. 44-47 (status word, control word); 5.6 register list p. 48; P0 list pp. 49-50; P1-11 and group 6 parameters pp. 52-59; trip codes 6.1 pp. 60-62"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Left out: register 6 (drive status). The guide describes it both as a 16-bit status word with bits 0-15 defined and as a single byte holding the last fault code, so its layout cannot be settled. Use register 9 for the trip code.",
    "Register 3 is not listed. Function 16 (write multiple) is accepted for registers 1-4 only; 03 and 06 work on the others.",
    "The guide states no signedness for most registers. Speed and analogue values that can go negative are typed INT16, counters and ratings UINT16.",
    "Registers 5, 40 and 42 use an 'IDL format' where 3000 = 50 Hz; they are kept raw.",
    "P6-02 (baud rate) is left out because the guide shows it in kbps (default 115) next to a 0-5 option list, so the stored value is unclear.",
    "Only the parameters an integrator needs for Modbus control are listed; every other parameter is reachable at its group-and-number register (for example 107 for P1-07).",
    "Trip codes listed are the A-class table; frame 3-5 drives with EN/UL 60730 certification also have class B trips."
  ],
